Chapter: IntMinLiteral

 A 64-bit immediate in the band i64-min..i64-min+254 was emitted as the
 wrong constant, with no diagnostic.

 `#8000000000000000` evaluated to 9223372036854775552, which is
 `0x7FFFFFFFFFFFFF00`. The front end was never at fault: lit-text-to-integer
 computes the value correctly, and the IR dump for such a definition reads
 `(int-lit i64-min)`. The loss happened one leaf function deep in the
 encoder. `write-bytes` extracts the eight little-endian bytes of an
 immediate through `floor-div`, which biased the dividend before dividing:

   if n >= 0 then n / d else (n - d + 1) / d

 For n = i64-min and d = 256 the subexpression `n - d + 1` underflows and
 wraps positive. The low byte still comes out right, because i64-min is
 divisible by 256; the quotient does not, so the remaining seven bytes are
 FF FF FF FF FF FF 7F. Reconstructing that little-endian gives exactly
 0x7FFFFFFFFFFFFF00, which is how the diagnosis was confirmed before the
 fix was written rather than after.

 The band ends where the underflow does. i64-min+255 subtracts to exactly
 i64-min and is representable, so it was always correct, and so was
 i64-min+256. Both are included here: a test that only covered the broken
 values would not have shown that the boundary is where the arithmetic says
 it is.

 The last three lines are the same defect seen through IEEE-754. The bit
 pattern of negative zero IS i64-min, so `bits-to-real` of that literal was
 handed a different double entirely, and every ordering answer about
 negative zero was an answer about some other number. That is what makes
 this worth a test rather than a curiosity: the wrong value is silent, and
 it reaches float code through the one pattern floats care about.

Section: Boundary

  b2i : Boolean -> Integer
  b2i (x) = if x then 1 else 0

Section: Report

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
    print-line-uni ("min       want -9223372036854775808 got " & show #8000000000000000)
    print-line-uni ("min+1     want -9223372036854775807 got " & show #8000000000000001)
    print-line-uni ("min+254   want -9223372036854775554 got " & show #80000000000000FE)
    print-line-uni ("min+255   want -9223372036854775553 got " & show #80000000000000FF)
    print-line-uni ("min+256   want -9223372036854775552 got " & show #8000000000000100)
    print-line-uni ("max       want 9223372036854775807 got " & show #7FFFFFFFFFFFFFFF)
    print-line-uni ("allf      want -1 got " & show #FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF)
    print-line-uni ("c000      want -4611686018427387904 got " & show #C000000000000000)
    print-line-uni ("minusinf  want -4503599627370496 got " & show #FFF0000000000000)
    print-line-uni ("shl63     want 1 got " & show (b2i (#8000000000000000 == bit-shl 1 63)))
    print-line-uni ("negzero   want 1 got " & show (b2i (real-to-bits (bits-to-real #8000000000000000) == bit-shl 1 63)))
    print-line-uni ("negzero>= want 1 got " & show (b2i (bits-to-real #8000000000000000 >= 0.0)))
    print-line-uni ("negzero<= want 1 got " & show (b2i (bits-to-real #8000000000000000 <= 0.0)))
  end
